> Full-width carry and exact work counts

For n=R−1 and reduced factors n−1, the exact REDC quotient before subtraction is
R. Its low64 bits are zero and its129th sum bit is set. The correct result is1.
This is a targeted boundary case where discarding the carry would return zero.
The table records that native event directly.

For n greater than1 and exponent e, the shared powering kernel makes two
conversion REDCs, L squares and H accumulator REDCs, where L is bit width and H
population count. It retains the final unused square. Thus total REDCs are2+L+H,
even at exponent zero where the two conversions remain. Modulus one is a
zero-result shortcut with no REDCs. This count is a word-operation model, not a
runtime comparison against division-based arithmetic.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/montgomery_work.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main() {
    std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
    auto n = std::numeric_limits<std::uint64_t>::max();
    dm::algorithms::MontgomeryContext full(n);
    auto t = full.reduce_trace(n - 1, n - 1);
    std::print("| modulus | reduced factor | carry | quotient low | subtracted | REDC result | ordinary " "product |\n| ---: | ---: | --- | ---: | --- | ---: | ---: |\n| {} | {} | {} | {} | {} | {} " "| {} |\n",
               n, n - 1, t.sum_carry, t.quotient_low, t.subtracted, t.result,
               full.multiply(n - 1, n - 1));
    std::vector<double> x, y;
    dm::algorithms::MontgomeryContext c(3233);
    std::print("\n| exponent | actual bit records | actual REDC calls | ordinary residue |\n| ---: | ---: | " "---: | ---: |\n");
    for (std::uint64_t e : {0ULL, 1ULL, 2ULL, 3ULL, 4ULL, 7ULL, 8ULL, 15ULL,
                            16ULL, 31ULL}) {
        auto p = c.power_trace(123, e);
        x.push_back(e);
        y.push_back(p.reductions);
        std::print("| {} | {} | {} | {} |\n", e, p.steps.size(), p.reductions,
                   p.result);
    }
    auto p = dm::graphics::RPlot::create();
    p.points(x, y, "actual REDC calls", {37, 99, 235}, 6).title(
        "Montgomery powers: loop and conversion work").x_label("exponent").y_label("REDC calls").save_svg("build/montgomery_work.svg");
}
```
