\caption(Actual full-width carry and powering work including conversions.)
\alttext(The targeted carry is retained and corrected to result1; powering counts include entry and exit.)

> Contracts and conclusion

The context accepts odd nonzero moduli, including one, and rejects zero or even
moduli before setup arithmetic. Ordinary multiply and power accept arbitrary
unsigned64-bit inputs; raw REDC methods require operands strictly below the
modulus. Trace capture owns its results. Power traces check complete effective
bit width against their default64-record cap before powering; zero disables the
cap. Context setup and raw products have constant fixed-word work/storage,
ordinary powering uses O(log exponent+1) operations and constant driver storage,
and its history adds O(log exponent+1) records.

The examples show the representation change, real setup costs, real conversion
costs and the full-width carry. They establish no CPU speed ratio or
constant-time guarantee. Secret-dependent branches, raw arithmetic and the tiny
RSA parameters require no interpretation as production cryptography.

[Montgomery, Modular multiplication without trial division (1985)|https://doi.org/10.1090/S0025-5718-1985-0777282-X]
supplies the reduction method. The explicit129-bit carry handling and context
capture contract describe this implementation.

> Verification

The ten-report batch passes95 CTest cases,31 directly instrumented ASan/UBSan
cases,83 compiled and executed public examples,363/363 scoped documentation
definitions and ten representative hovers. Independent Python integer
arithmetic, MT19937-64/variation replay, graph sets, analytic interpolation,
circle boundary enumeration and actual-sample integration reconstruction agree
on915459 captured records. All six original RMS summaries are separately checked
using96 native MISER estimates and1600000 independently reproduced
plain-comparator points. Frozen valid-input comparisons include the original
seeded solver paths and full MOEA/D fronts. Ten checkout headers and ten
identically installed development headers compile independently, and an
installed-header native consumer links and runs. Each report has four executed
complete programs, four reviewed native figures and both HTML/Markdown exports
with computed-result and image-byte checks. This is a scoped native API audit,
not an installation claim for every language binding. Receipts:
`build/mepml-conversion/batch-234-243/`.
